<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego de Losada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511–1569</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego de Losada was a Spanish conquistador who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Santiago de León de Caracas</a> in 1567, after campaigning against the Indigenous peoples of the valley. Born in the kingdom of León, he had served in Venezuela for many years. Caracas became the capital of the Province of Venezuela in 1578.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-de-losada.jpg" alt="Diego de Losada" width="320" height="612" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio Herrera Toro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diego_de_Losada_-_Antonio_Herrera_Toro_Concejo_Municipal_de_Caracas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
